  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "uniequip_001_swllow",
      "name": {
        "en": "GreyThroat's Badge",
        "zh": "灰喉证章",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "INITIAL",
      "typeName2": "",
      "icon": "original",
      "description": {
        "en": "Operator GreyThroat has demonstrated a remarkable aptitude for maintaining distance whilst conducting suppressive fire against the enemy.\nThe Field Operations Department has thus passed the following resolution:\nThis operator shall be appointed a Sniper Operator during field operations to exercise Marksman responsibilities.\nIn witness whereof,\nThis badge is hereby conferred upon the above named.",
        "zh": "干员灰喉擅长保持距离对敌人进行火力压制\n根据外勤部门决议\n在外勤任务中划分为狙击干员，行使速射手职责\n特别颁发此证章\n以兹证明",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "uniequip_002_swllow",
      "name": {
        "en": "Reflection of a Mother's Love",
        "zh": "母爱的倒影",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "ADVANCED",
      "typeName2": "Y",
      "icon": "uniequip_002_swllow",
      "description": {
        "en": "She comes to in the corridor where she played as a child. She remembers; her father's working very late today. She's waiting in the corridor for him. The sunset clouds are chased in by autumn winds, and in this country town where no high-rise nor skyscraper stands, time's gifts are ever there to be seized at the first moments. Quietly, she pushes her father's door open and sees his stern expression—something has happened, her child's instincts say.\nShe comes to in the crook of her mother's arm. She remembers; she is nine now. She should be celebrating her birthday with her friends, sharing the cake. There should be candles aflame, yet the town burns. She sees her mother's face; in the instant she notices her daughter's gaze, the enmity and apprehension is hidden away behind the moon. The night is deep and dark, and her mother tells her it'll all be alright.\nShe comes to in a tent in the barrens. She remembers; this is their third month on the run. The incident in town seemed to serve as an excuse for all the other relatives to shun the mother and daughter. Her faith in and dependence on others left her in the sound of a single crash. She hasn't seen her father for so long now. She dearly wishes to cry and cry, and so she hugs her mother, but droplets hit the floor before she's even begun to weep.\nShe comes to beneath an unfamiliar carport. She remembers; her tenth birthday is very soon. Surrounding her are adults as frigid as ice, one by one forcing out a smile. She is a smart child, and knows these people mean well, but she's only a child all the same. The adults tell her that her mother is entrusting her to Rhodes Island. Her mother has left, like a cloud.\nShe comes to in brand-new bedding. She remembers; her arm is filled with bruising. She used a stolen sheet of sandpaper to rub at her once-smooth skin, hounding the flesh as though it'd atone. It hurts, and she dares not continue, but the moment she thinks of the black crystals, her throat is in the death grip of an all-choking emotion. She wants to vomit. She can't. She hasn't eaten in so very, very long.\nShe comes to the boom of floodwater. She remembers; Amiya and the Infected are still below. Those nameless heroes are resisting a mere Catastrophe. She lifts her head, and as the elements batter all, it suddenly strikes her that suffering is not a matter of great or small, and nor is hope. She throws herself down. Amiya must be alright, at the very least. She hears those behind her howling in fear. She hears them. Infected are drowning here, they say; when the flood recedes, will their water sources be polluted?\nShe comes to beneath a sunset as red as fire. She remembers; she saved a great many at Sugar City, a great many more than she could know. Her mother comes to mind. All at once, she feels sad, yet smiles. She understands her father, but still hasn't been able to find her mother. Can she find her? Will she ever? As the thought strikes her, she has a mild headache, but feels unusually unburdened.\nShe turns her head, and gives the great Feline as badly wounded as her a tremendous chewing-out. 'Blaze! Can't you wake me up any other way?!'",
        "zh": "她在儿时玩耍的走廊醒来。她记起来，今天父亲下班很晚。她在走廊上等父亲。晚霞被秋风捎来，没有高楼大厦的乡野小镇，总能第一时间捕捉到时间的馈赠。她悄悄推开父亲的房门，看着父亲严肃的面庞——孩子的直觉告诉她，有什么事已经发生了。\n她在母亲的臂弯中醒来。她记起来，她已经九岁了。她本该和伙伴们庆祝生日，分着蛋糕。燃烧的应当是蜡烛，而非城镇。她看着母亲的脸，在意识到女儿视线的瞬间，那些仇恨与疑虑全都被藏在了月亮后面。夜色很深，母亲告诉她，都会没事的。\n她在荒野的帐篷里醒来。她记起来，这已经是他们逃出来的第三个月。那场发生在小镇的变故，似乎成为了亲戚们将母女二人拒之门外的借口。咣当一声关上的，是年幼的她对人们的信任与依赖。她已经很久没见过父亲了，她很想大哭一场，于是她抱向母亲，可她还没来得及哭，水滴就落在地上。\n她在陌生的车棚下醒来。她记起来，马上就要到她的十岁生日了。周围都是冷冰冰的大人，他们挨个挤出笑脸。她是个聪明的孩子，她其实知道这些人没有恶意，但她毕竟只是个孩子。大人们告诉她，她的母亲将她委托给了罗德岛。她的母亲离开了，像一朵云。\n她在崭新的被褥中醒来。她记起来，她的手臂上满是伤痕。她用偷来的砂纸打磨原本光滑的皮肤，皮开肉绽。她很疼，她不敢继续，但一想到那些黑色的结晶，弥漫的情绪就死死扼住了咽喉。她想吐，吐不出，她已经很久没好好吃饭了。\n她在洪水的轰鸣中醒来。她记起来，阿米娅和那些感染者还在下面。那些无名英雄对抗的只是天灾，她仰头，风雨洗刷，她忽地觉得，苦难并不分轻重，希望亦然。她纵身跳下，至少，阿米娅不能出事。她听见身后的人们在惊恐吼叫，他们说，感染者淹没在水里，洪水退去，水源会不会被污染？\n她在如火的夕阳下醒来。她记起来，她在甘糖城救下了很多人，很多很多人。她想起了自己的母亲，她忽感悲伤，却又笑了。她理解了父亲，可还没能找到她的母亲。她能找到吗？她会找到吗？想到这，她略感头痛，但出奇轻松。\n她转过头去，对着那个同样受伤不轻的大菲林大骂道：“煌！你就不能换个办法叫醒我吗？”",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
